  "quote_of_the_week": {
    "type": "Quote of the Week",
    "quote": "You pray for rain; you have to deal with the mud too. That's a part of it.",
    "author": "Denzel Washington (born 28 December 1954) - American actor, director & two times Oscar winner."
  },
  "market_commentary": {
    "overview": "",
    "bulkers": "One more active sale and purchase week with Chinese buyers again in the spotlight: Chinese \ninterests acquired the capesize vessels STAR SCARLETT (175k dwt built 2014 at Jinhai/China) for a \nfirm $ 36 million and SMYRNA (176k dwt built 2008 at Namura/Japan) for $ 25.3 mill. They are also \nnegotiating the purchase of the scrubber-fitted kamsarmax sisters ANGLO BARINTHUS & ANGLO \nRED (81k dwt bult 2013 at Sainty/China) for $ 17 million each, either with balance of period index t/c \nattached to Klaveness or on a charter-free basis for delivery mid-late March. For comparison, the exact \nsister vessel, THERESA HAINAN, was sold in December last year for a price in the low to mid $16 \nmillion range.  \n \nClients of Niovis have bought the supramax vessel LUMINA (56k dwt built 2015 at Mitsui/Japan) for \n$ 22 million establishing a new market benchmark. Clients of Lomar have disposed supramax LIMA \nTRADER (Dolphin 57 design built at 2012 Qingshan/China) for $ 13.2 million, while \nsmaller LIANSON DYNAMIC (Diamond 53 design built 2006 at Chengxi/China) sold for a price \nregion high $8 - $9 mill. In an auction sale organized last week by the High Court of Gujarat in India, \nsupramax ELVITA R (53k dwt built at Zhejiang/China) went under the hammer for $8.95 mill.  \n \nThe highly sought-after design \"B-Delta\" Eco handysize POWAN (39.7k dwt built 2016 at \nOuhua/China) was snapped by Greek buyers for a whopping $19.2 mill. Smaller handy SIGMA \nVENTURE (35k built 2012 at Chengxi/China) changed hands for $11.75 million.",
    "tankers": "Sinokor's shopping frenzy continues as they are linked with three VLCC acquisitions this \nweek: sisters INGRID & ILMA (314k dwt built 2012 Hyundai/South Korea) for $89 mill a piece and \nEAGLE VARNA (300k dwt built 2013 DSME/South Korea) for $ 86.5 million. These levels represent \na substantial price increase compared to the en bloc sale of slightly bigger sisters DELTA GLORY & \nDELTA ANGELICA (320k dwt built 2012 at Hyundai/South Korea) which were sold for $80 million \neach in early January. \nSuezmax NORDIC POLLUX (150k dwt built 2003 at Universal/Japan) went for $ 25 mill, a price in \nline with en bloc sale of one-year younger sisters NORDIC LUNA & NORDIC SPRINTER (150k \ndwt built 2004 at Universal/Japan) for $25 mill each in early January.  \nAframax NORDSYMPHONY (106k dwt built 2008 at Tsuneishi/Japan) attracted $ 35.5 mill, same \nprice as one-year younger sister IONIC ARTEMIS (107k dwt built 2009 at Tsuneishi/Japan) achieved \nin late January.",
    "demolition": "Subcontinent rates are stable this week with a positive outlook. For an overview of \ndemolition market rates, please check our comprehensive demometer below:"
  },
